4T15:24:54.389Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Checking formatting...\nAll matched files use Prettier code style!\ndiff --git a/src/commands/extendLock-2.lua b/src/commands/extendLock-2.lua\nindex 2d5ffe3..37a3e30 100644\n--- a/src/commands/extendLock-2.lua\n+++ b/src/commands/extendLock-2.lua\n@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@\n     \"1\" if lock extended successfully.\n ]]\n local rcall = redis.call\n-if rcall(\"EXISTS\", KEYS[1]) == 1 then\n+if rcall(\"GET\", KEYS[1]) == ARGV[1] then\n   --   if rcall(\"SET\", KEYS[1], ARGV[1], \"PX\", ARGV[2], \"XX\") then\n   if rcall(\"SET\", KEYS[1], ARGV[1], \"PX\", ARGV[2]) then\n     rcall(\"SREM\", KEYS[2], ARGV[3])\ndiff --git a/src/commands/extendLocks-1.lua b/src/commands/extendLocks-1.lua\nindex cce23e6..bbd5548 100644\n--- a/src/commands/extendLocks-1.lua\n+++ b/src/commands/extendLocks-1.lua\n@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ for i = 1, jobCount, 1 do\n \n     local currentToken = rcall(\"GET\", lockKey)\n     if currentToken then\n-        if currentToken then\n+        if currentToken == token then\n             local setResult = rcall(\"SET\", lockKey, token, \"PX\", lockDuration)\n             if setResult then\n                 rcall(\"SREM\", stalledKey, jobId)\ndiff --git a/src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua b/src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua\nindex b8025cc..d7335f6 100644\n--- a/src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua\n+++ b/src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ local function removeLock(jobKey, stalledKey, token, jobId)\n   if token ~= \"0\" then\n     local lockKey = jobKey .. ':lock'\n     local lockToken = rcall(\"GET\", lockKey)\n-    if lockToken then\n+    if lockToken == token then\n       rcall(\"DEL\", lockKey)\n       rcall(\"SREM\", stalledKey, jobId)\n     else","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhRqd2MKncfBpPNouikJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The regression is fixed: a stale worker can no longer complete, fail, retry, delay or renew a job that another worker has recovered. The prevalidated regression command plus the new test file passes (276 tests, 8 files, exit 0), and `npm run build` succeeds.\n\n## Cause\n\nThree Redis Lua scripts checked only that a lock existed, not that the caller's token owned it:\n\n- **`src/commands/includes/removeLock.lua`** — shared by complete/fail, immediate retry, delayed retry, move-to-wait and move-to-waiting-children. It deleted whatever lock was present, so the stale worker released the new owner's lock and went on to change the job. It now requires `lockToken == token`, returning `-6` (lock mismatch) or `-2` (missing lock) as the existing API defines.\n- **`src/commands/extendLock-2.lua`** — overwrote the current owner's lock with the caller's token. It now renews only when the stored token matches, and returns `0` otherwise.\n- **`src/commands/extendLocks-1.lua`** — same problem in the batch path. Non-owned jobs are now reported in the failed-ids list and left untouched.\n\nEach fix is a one-line condition change. The token `\"0\"` bypass used by administrative APIs is unchanged, and the stalled-job recovery script was not touched. The Postgres backend already did these checks correctly.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **New tests:** I added `tests/stale_worker_ownership.redis.test.ts` (8 tests). It puts a job through real lock expiry and stalled recovery, then has the stale worker try each operation. Seven of the eight fail on the original code and all pass with the fix.\n- **Rejection leaves the job untouched:** the tests assert the lock-mismatch error and that state, attempt counters, result, failure reason, delay, lock owner and event-stream length are identical before and after.\n- **Owner still works:** the current owner can still renew, complete, fail, retry immediately and retry with fixed backoff.\n- **Missing lock:** a missing lock is still a \"missing lock\" error on completion and `0` on renewal.\n\nOne behaviour I left as it was: `retryJob` promotes any due delayed jobs before it checks the lock, so a rejected stale retry can still emit events for other jobs that were due. It never touches the contested job; say if you want that moved after the ownership check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1060,"cache_read_input_tokens":69661,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1060},"output_tokens":695,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1897958-d059-4bf2-a643-0cfa35d14c6d","uuid":"97b8a0f5-af57-4637-87d3-68cbaadebd57","timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:25:03.498Z","request_id":"req_011CfhRqcjEw2zU4Wz6Apn9x"}
